Subject: [PATCH 2/2] claude/skills/freebsd-port: Build ports, never deps
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: zxquunzwoynkosszuskvmpzprxryqovr

Ports have gone to the list without a build, so the build and the
plist were first checked in Pat's poudriere run, a round trip later.
A vendored module that no longer compiles with the tree's Go, or a
plist drafted from upstream's install rules, passes every linter and
fails only there.

Building the port itself is cheap; what took too long was building
its dependencies. port-make.sh never does that, so the skill now
builds, stages, and runs check-plist through it. When dependencies are
missing, the skill answers with the whole list instead of posting an
unbuilt patch, so the operator can install them in one step and run
it again.
